I know this has been discussed many times before but to be sure...  So,
xorxes, you would use {ji'i} in a way such that {li re ji'i pa} would be
understood to mean what exactly?  Some actual number that is definitely
twenty something, and it's around 21 (so it cannot be 19 but 24 would be
reasonable)?

And how is this different from how the CLL prescribes?

So in your understanding of {ji'i}, if I wanted to say "about 10" would I
have to say {li ji'i pano}.  Would this mean "0, 10, 20, or 30" or "8, 9,
10, 11, or 12".  (i.e. would the ji'i apply to only the pa, or would it
apply to pano).  Or am I completely mis-understanding how PA4 works for
{ji'i}?

2010/11/4 Jorge Llamb=EDas <jjllambias@gmail.com>

